{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-39526","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43367","text":"Graphonomous × box-and-box — Arithmetic Compliance Review"}]},{"id":"blk-39527","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43368","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-43369","text":" review (no behavior change) · "},{"id":"spn-43370","marks":["bold"],"text":"Kernel:"},{"id":"spn-43371","text":" "},{"id":"spn-43372","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-43373","text":" v0.8.0 (8 rungs, 97 laws) "},{"id":"spn-43374","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope:"},{"id":"spn-43375","text":" how closely the Graphonomous memory engine (OS-001) already conforms to the [&] governance kernel, rung by rung, and the small set of *additive* naming/wiring changes that would make it explicitly compliant."}]},{"id":"blk-39528","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43376","text":"TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-39529","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43377","text":"Graphonomous is "},{"id":"spn-43378","marks":["bold"],"text":"already structurally isomorphic"},{"id":"spn-43379","text":" to the kernel's load-bearing rungs — it just doesn't *name* them. Its coverage→decision policy is the bridge ("},{"id":"spn-43380","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-43381","text":"); its coverage score is the axiological semiring; its Wilson intervals are the epistemic rung; its cost cap is the resource rung's affine ledger. The gap is "},{"id":"spn-43382","marks":["bold"],"text":"vocabulary + two small guarantees"},{"id":"spn-43383","text":", not architecture. Nothing here requires a core refactor; every recommendation is additive."}]},{"id":"blk-39530","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43384","text":"Compliance scorecard"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-39532","spans":[{"id":"spn-43385","text":"Kernel rung"}]},{"id":"blk-39533","spans":[{"id":"spn-43386","text":"Graphonomous implementation"}]},{"id":"blk-39534","spans":[{"id":"spn-43387","text":"Compliance"}]}],"id":"blk-39531","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-39535","spans":[{"id":"spn-43388","text":"1. alethic ("},{"id":"spn-43389","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-43390","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-39536","spans":[{"id":"spn-43391","marks":["code"],"text":"Topology.compute_kappa/2"},{"id":"spn-43392","text":", SCC analysis; node confidence"}]},{"id":"blk-39537","spans":[{"id":"spn-43393","text":"✅ ~90% — κ is a first-class Value"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39538","spans":[{"id":"spn-43394","text":"2. axiological ("},{"id":"spn-43395","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-43396","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-39539","spans":[{"id":"spn-43397","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.weighted_sum/2"},{"id":"spn-43398","text":", "},{"id":"spn-43399","marks":["code"],"text":"Reranker"}]},{"id":"blk-39540","spans":[{"id":"spn-43400","text":"◻ ~60% — weighted sum, not a *named* semiring"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39541","spans":[{"id":"spn-43401","text":"3. deontic (norm/govern)"}]},{"id":"blk-39542","spans":[{"id":"spn-43402","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.pick_decision/4"},{"id":"spn-43403","text":" floor gates (act/learn/escalate)"}]},{"id":"blk-39543","spans":[{"id":"spn-43404","text":"◻ ~70% — floor present, "},{"id":"spn-43405","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-43406","text":" veto implicit"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39544","spans":[{"id":"spn-43407","text":"4. temporal (LTL ▸ supervise)"}]},{"id":"blk-39545","spans":[{"id":"spn-43408","text":"consolidation cadence; freshness/staleness decay"}]},{"id":"blk-39546","spans":[{"id":"spn-43409","text":"◻ ~40% — time-aware, no LTL obligations"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39547","spans":[{"id":"spn-43410","text":"5. reflexive (entrenched ring-0)"}]},{"id":"blk-39548","spans":[{"id":"spn-43411","text":"— (no self-amendment surface)"}]},{"id":"blk-39549","spans":[{"id":"spn-43412","text":"✕ out of scope"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39550","spans":[{"id":"spn-43413","text":"6. epistemic (knows ▸ believes)"}]},{"id":"blk-39551","spans":[{"id":"spn-43414","marks":["code"],"text":"Uncertainty.interval/1"},{"id":"spn-43415","text":" (Wilson), "},{"id":"spn-43416","marks":["code"],"text":"BeliefRevision"},{"id":"spn-43417","text":" (AGM)"}]},{"id":"blk-39552","spans":[{"id":"spn-43418","text":"✅ ~95% — strongest rung"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39553","spans":[{"id":"spn-43419","text":"7. strategic (coalition power)"}]},{"id":"blk-39554","spans":[{"id":"spn-43420","text":"— (single-agent; delegated to Deliberatic)"}]},{"id":"blk-39555","spans":[{"id":"spn-43421","text":"✕ out of scope"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39556","spans":[{"id":"spn-43422","text":"8. resource (affine ledger)"}]},{"id":"blk-39557","spans":[{"id":"spn-43423","marks":["code"],"text":"CostTracker.budget_exceeded?/0"},{"id":"spn-43424","text":" ($10/day), "},{"id":"spn-43425","marks":["code"],"text":"Forgetter"},{"id":"spn-43426","text":" LRU+decay"}]},{"id":"blk-39558","spans":[{"id":"spn-43427","text":"◻ ~85% — ledger present"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-39559","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43428","text":"Rung-by-rung detail (grounded in the code)"}]},{"id":"blk-39560","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43429","text":"Rung 1 — alethic ("},{"id":"spn-43430","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-43431","text":") ✅"}]},{"id":"blk-39561","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43432","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/topology.ex"},{"id":"spn-43433","text":" "},{"id":"spn-43434","marks":["code"],"text":"compute_kappa/2"},{"id":"spn-43435","text":" (line 134) computes the "},{"id":"spn-43436","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ cyclicity invariant"},{"id":"spn-43437","text":" — the same Value-family invariant the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-43438","marks":["code"],"text":"value.mjs"},{"id":"spn-43439","text":" carries (alethic \"what can happen\"). Node confidence scores are the truth-degrees over which Value laws "},{"id":"spn-43440","marks":["code"],"text":"L1–L14"},{"id":"spn-43441","text":" range. "},{"id":"spn-43442","marks":["bold"],"text":"Already compliant"},{"id":"spn-43443","text":"; recommend citing the rung-1 correspondence in the "},{"id":"spn-43444","marks":["code"],"text":"Topology"},{"id":"spn-43445","text":" moduledoc so κ is understood as the alethic Value, not a bespoke metric."}]},{"id":"blk-39562","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43446","text":"Rung 2 — axiological ("},{"id":"spn-43447","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-43448","text":") ◻ → name the semiring"}]},{"id":"blk-39563","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43449","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/coverage.ex"},{"id":"spn-43450","text":" "},{"id":"spn-43451","marks":["code"],"text":"weighted_sum/2"},{"id":"spn-43452","text":" (line 604) computes "},{"id":"spn-43453","marks":["code"],"text":"Σ value × weight"},{"id":"spn-43454","text":" and clamps to "},{"id":"spn-43455","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,1]"},{"id":"spn-43456","text":". That is the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-43457","marks":["bold"],"text":"probability semiring"},{"id":"spn-43458","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-43459","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = +"},{"id":"spn-43460","text":", "},{"id":"spn-43461","marks":["code"],"text":"⊗ = ×"},{"id":"spn-43462","text":") from "},{"id":"spn-43463","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-43464","text":". "},{"id":"spn-43465","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-43466","text":" document that the coverage score *is* the axiological rung in the probability semiring, and (optionally) expose a tropical ("},{"id":"spn-43467","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = min"},{"id":"spn-43468","text":") \"weakest-component\" view alongside the weighted mean — so the engine can answer \"is any coverage component failing?\" the way the kernel's safety floor does, not just \"how good on average?\"."}]},{"id":"blk-39564","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43469","text":"Rung 3 — deontic (norm/govern) ◻ → make the "},{"id":"spn-43470","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-43471","text":" veto explicit"}]},{"id":"blk-39565","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43472","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.pick_decision/4"},{"id":"spn-43473","text":" (line 392) is "},{"id":"spn-43474","marks":["bold"],"text":"the bridge, already implemented"},{"id":"spn-43475","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-39566","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":act  when coverage ≥ floor  AND uncertainty ≤ ceiling  AND risk ≤ ceiling   # feasible ▸ permitted\n:learn when (looser floor)                                                    # permitted, not yet best\n:escalate otherwise                                                           # floor not met"},{"id":"blk-39567","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43476","text":"This is exactly "},{"id":"spn-43477","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-43478","text":": the conjunctive thresholds are the "},{"id":"spn-43479","marks":["bold"],"text":"un-weakenable safety floor"},{"id":"spn-43480","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-43481","marks":["code"],"text":"decision_confidence/3"},{"id":"spn-43482","text":" (line 409) is the "},{"id":"spn-43483","marks":["bold"],"text":"gradient"},{"id":"spn-43484","text":" that the bridge's "},{"id":"spn-43485","marks":["code"],"text":"best"},{"id":"spn-43486","text":" step optimizes. The one missing guarantee is "},{"id":"spn-43487","marks":["bold"],"text":"`0̲` annihilation"},{"id":"spn-43488","text":": in the kernel, a floor violation *annihilates* the verdict (no amount of gradient can rescue it). Graphonomous approximates this — "},{"id":"spn-43489","marks":["code"],"text":":escalate"},{"id":"spn-43490","text":" is terminal — but the relationship is implicit. "},{"id":"spn-43491","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-43492","text":" state in the "},{"id":"spn-43493","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage"},{"id":"spn-43494","text":" moduledoc that a sub-floor signal annihilates to "},{"id":"spn-43495","marks":["code"],"text":":escalate"},{"id":"spn-43496","text":" (the deontic "},{"id":"spn-43497","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-43498","text":"), and add a property test mirroring the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-43499","marks":["code"],"text":"DB2"},{"id":"spn-43500","text":" annihilation law so the guarantee can't silently regress."}]},{"id":"blk-39568","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43501","text":"Rung 4 — temporal (LTL ▸ supervise) ◻"}]},{"id":"blk-39569","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43502","text":"Freshness/staleness decay ("},{"id":"spn-43503","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage.ex"},{"id":"spn-43504","text":" line 383) and consolidation cadence are time-aware, but there are no explicit LTL obligations (e.g. \"every stored contradiction is *eventually* resolved\"). "},{"id":"spn-43505","marks":["bold"],"text":"Out of scope to add now"},{"id":"spn-43506","text":"; flagged as the natural next rung if temporal guarantees become first-class. Maps to "},{"id":"spn-43507","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/temporal.mjs"},{"id":"spn-43508","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-43509","marks":["code"],"text":"X"},{"id":"spn-43510","text":", "},{"id":"spn-43511","marks":["code"],"text":"◇"},{"id":"spn-43512","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-39570","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43513","text":"Rung 6 — epistemic (knows ▸ believes) ✅ strongest"}]},{"id":"blk-39571","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43514","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/uncertainty.ex"},{"id":"spn-43515","text":" "},{"id":"spn-43516","marks":["code"],"text":"interval/1"},{"id":"spn-43517","text":" (line 28) computes "},{"id":"spn-43518","marks":["bold"],"text":"Wilson confidence intervals"},{"id":"spn-43519","text":" over evidence counts, with an explicit "},{"id":"spn-43520","marks":["code"],"text":":no_evidence"},{"id":"spn-43521","text":" bottom — this is the kernel's epistemic rung (S5/KD45 \"knows ▸ believes\") in statistical form. "},{"id":"spn-43522","marks":["code"],"text":"BeliefRevision"},{"id":"spn-43523","text":" implements "},{"id":"spn-43524","marks":["bold"],"text":"AGM"},{"id":"spn-43525","text":" expansion/contraction with "},{"id":"spn-43526","marks":["code"],"text":"contradicts"},{"id":"spn-43527","text":" edges. "},{"id":"spn-43528","marks":["bold"],"text":"Already compliant"},{"id":"spn-43529","text":" at ~95%; recommend naming the "},{"id":"spn-43530","marks":["code"],"text":":no_evidence"},{"id":"spn-43531","text":" case as the epistemic bottom and citing the rung-6 correspondence. This is the rung Graphonomous could claim conformance on today."}]},{"id":"blk-39572","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43532","text":"Rung 8 — resource (affine ledger) ◻"}]},{"id":"blk-39573","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43533","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/cost_tracker.ex"},{"id":"spn-43534","text":" "},{"id":"spn-43535","marks":["code"],"text":"budget_exceeded?/0"},{"id":"spn-43536","text":" (line 167) enforces a "},{"id":"spn-43537","marks":["code"],"text":"$10/day"},{"id":"spn-43538","text":" cap — an "},{"id":"spn-43539","marks":["bold"],"text":"affine ledger"},{"id":"spn-43540","text":": spend is consumed and cannot go negative past the cap. The "},{"id":"spn-43541","marks":["code"],"text":"Forgetter"},{"id":"spn-43542","text":" (LRU + priority decay) is resource reclamation. This is the kernel's resource rung ("},{"id":"spn-43543","marks":["code"],"text":"resource.mjs"},{"id":"spn-43544","text":", laws "},{"id":"spn-43545","marks":["code"],"text":"C1–C8"},{"id":"spn-43546","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-43547","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-43548","text":" emit the daily-budget remaining as a resource signal and name it with the resource-rung vocabulary ("},{"id":"spn-43549","marks":["code"],"text":"consume"},{"id":"spn-43550","text":", overspend → "},{"id":"spn-43551","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-43552","text":"), so unattended autonomy degrades gracefully via the same algebra the kernel uses."}]},{"id"